## One-Time Car Inspection Before Purchase in Serbia — Honda Accord 2024

Yuri reached out to us requesting a one-time car inspection before purchasing a vehicle in Serbia. He was interested in a **2024 Honda Accord** with a mileage of about **30,000 kilometers**.

Before finalizing the purchase, we conducted a comprehensive technical and visual inspection to assess the true condition of the Honda Accord and identify any potential flaws that might not be apparent during a standard check.

During the pre-purchase inspection, we performed the following:

- computer diagnostics of all major electronic systems of the vehicle;
- checking for errors and recorded malfunctions in the control units;
- engine diagnostics and assessment of its performance;
- inspecting the engine compartment for signs of oil and other fluids;
- checking the level and condition of operational fluids;
- visual inspection of the body and all elements of the vehicle;
- measuring the thickness of the paint coating to identify painted or repaired parts;
- checking the body for signs of accidents, repairs, and part replacements;
- assessing the condition of headlights, windows, body gaps, and exterior elements;
- inspecting the suspension and components of the chassis;
- checking the braking system;
- examining the condition of tires and rims;
- looking at the vehicle's undercarriage;
- checking for corrosion, damage, and signs of wear;
- a test drive to evaluate the engine, transmission, suspension, and brakes;
- assessing the overall technical condition of the vehicle and potential investments needed after purchase.

We paid particular attention to ensuring that the declared mileage matched the actual condition of the vehicle. The inspection also included evaluating the state of the body, interior, engine, chassis, and other key components of the **Honda Accord**.

As a result of the inspection, Yuri received objective information on the condition of the vehicle and was able to make a purchase decision based on not just the seller's word, but also the results of professional diagnostics.

Additionally, during negotiations, we successfully managed to reduce the initial price of the car by **700 euros**.

A one-time car inspection before purchase is a convenient service for those who have found a vehicle on their own in Serbia but want to ensure its technical condition and legal transparency before handing over money to the seller.

If you have found a Honda, BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Volkswagen, Škoda, Toyota, or any other make of car in Serbia, don’t rush to hand over money to the seller. A professional one-time inspection can help uncover hidden flaws and provide a solid basis for negotiation.

